      "title": "Public confidence in judicial authority must be continuously earned: CJI",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/public-confidence-in-judicial-authority-must-be-continuously-earned-cji-126112600570_1.html",
      "description": "Chief Justice of India Surya Kant on Thursday said a confident institution must have the capacity to engage with criticism without treating every disagreement as a challenge to its authority, underlining that disagreement is not a weakness of a constitutional democracy.\nAddressing a Constitution Day function organised by the Supreme Court Bar Association (SCBA) at the apex court lawns, the CJI also said that the Constitution is not tested only during extraordinary political or institutional crises, but it is tested every day.\n\"It is tested every day, in the ordinary exercise of power. The manner in which an authority treats a vulnerable citizen, the willingness of an institution to acknowledge its limitations, and the readiness to correct an error are all expressions of constitutional commitment,\" the CJI said.\nThe CJI said a confident institution must have the capacity to engage with criticism without treating every disagreement as a challenge to its authority.\n\"What matters is th",
